D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   ],

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   "source": [

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "# Loop through each fitted LogisticRegression model\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "for i, model in enumerate(clf.estimators_):\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    \n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    class_label = clf.classes_[i]\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    \n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    # Extract the weights and bias\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    # Note: .coef_ returns a 2D array of shape (1, n_features), so we grab index [0]\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    weights = model.coef_[0] \n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    bias = model.intercept_[0]\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    \n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    print(f\"--- Model for Class: {class_label} ---\")\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    print(f\"Weights: {weights}\")\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "    print(f\"Intercept: {bias}\\n\")"

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   ]

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->  },

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->  {

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   "cell_type": "markdown",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   "id": "3d7d2839",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   "metadata": {},

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   "source": [

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "### Note\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "- Logistic Regression is a linear model. It tries to draw straight lines (or flat planes) through our data to separate the classes. If Class 1 or Class 3 is scattered wildly amongst Class 0, a straight line will never be able to separate them, no matter how much we resample the data.\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "\n",

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->    "- SMOTE is undeniably working better than the class_weight approach, but we have hit the ceiling of what Logistic Regression can do with our current features."

D:\UniPi\Semester 1\420AA Data Mining\Project DM2\Data-Mining-2-2026->   ]

